    {
      "id": "LHXmf7Xosjzl3VEJZSFRJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1794.9591279207384,
      "y": 1918.7635919850609,
      "width": 1512.0269806749857,
      "height": 1035,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 695870720,
      "version": 240,
      "versionNonce": 636922624,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775158023520,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. DDL (Data Definition Language) Commands that define database structure -\nCREATE, ALTER, DROP tables, indexes, and constraints. Changes the database\nschema.\n\n2. CREATE EXTENSION pgcrypto Adds PostgreSQL's cryptography functions for\nhashing, encryption, and generating random UUIDs. Like installing a plugin for security\nfeatures.\n\n3. DDL Script A file containing DDL commands to set up database structure -\ncreates tables, indexes, constraints. Runs once to build the database schema.\n\n4. UUID vs user_id id UUID PRIMARY KEY creates a unique random identifier that's\nglobally unique and hard to guess. user_id would require manual management and could\nconflict.\n\n5. Indexes & Triggers\n\nIndex: Speeds up data retrieval like a book index. CREATE INDEX idx_email ON\nusers(email);\nTrigger: Automatic action when data changes. Your example runs\nupdate_modified_column() before any user update, automatically setting a modified\ntimestamp.\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. DDL (Data Definition Language) Commands that define database structure - CREATE, ALTER, DROP tables, indexes, and constraints. Changes the database schema.\n\n2. CREATE EXTENSION pgcrypto Adds PostgreSQL's cryptography functions for hashing, encryption, and generating random UUIDs. Like installing a plugin for security features.\n\n3. DDL Script A file containing DDL commands to set up database structure - creates tables, indexes, constraints. Runs once to build the database schema.\n\n4. UUID vs user_id id UUID PRIMARY KEY creates a unique random identifier that's globally unique and hard to guess. user_id would require manual management and could conflict.\n\n5. Indexes & Triggers\n\nIndex: Speeds up data retrieval like a book index. CREATE INDEX idx_email ON users(email);\nTrigger: Automatic action when data changes. Your example runs update_modified_column() before any user update, automatically setting a modified timestamp.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
